# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/courses_more.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event evo_fog_to_the_line
# en: Fog to the Line
title [db3387] = 雾到线为止
# en: {Professor Thorne chalks a line on the wall at shoulder height. "Water and fire together. Make fog. To the line, and not a hair over."|Fog day. Thorne's chalk line is lower than last time.|The fog line again. Thorne no longer explains; he just draws it and folds his arms.} {The windows have been shut.|Somebody's fog smells of burnt toast.|{season == "winter": The fog freezes on the windows in ferns.|The hall is warm, and the fog comes too easily.}}
text [b72f54] = {索恩教授在墙上齐肩高处画了一道粉笔线。“水与火并用。造雾。到线为止，多一根头发都不行。”|造雾日。索恩的粉笔线比上回低了。|又是雾线。索恩不再解释；他只是画好线，抱起胳膊。} {窗户都关上了。|有人的雾闻起来像烤焦的吐司。|{season == "winter": 雾在窗上冻成了蕨叶。|大厅里很暖，雾来得太容易。}}
# en: A lecture hall filling slowly with white fog from students' hands, a chalk line drawn on the wall at shoulder height, a stern old professor holding a measuring stick.
scene [9f8962] = 讲堂里学生们手中缓缓涌出白雾，墙上齐肩高处画着一道粉笔线，一位严厉的老教授握着一根量尺。
# en: Balance fire and water exactly
opt.left.label [7ee0f3] = 精准平衡水与火
# en: {Your fog rises, thick and white, and stops at the line as if it can read. Thorne looks at it a long time. "Hm."|Your fog fills the hall to the chalk precisely. Thorne makes a small mark in his book; you'd give a crown to know what.|You hold the balance so finely that your fog comes up the wall like a tide and stops. Thorne nods, once. From him, a standing ovation.}
opt.left.say.1 [b6f29d] = {你的雾升起来，浓而白，到线就停，仿佛识字。索恩盯着它看了很久。“嗯。”|你的雾不多不少正好灌到粉笔线。索恩在本子上做了个小记号；你愿意出一个克朗知道写了什么。|你把平衡掌握得极精，雾像潮水一样爬上墙，然后停住。索恩点了一次头。对他来说，这就是起立鼓掌。}
# en: {Too much fire. Your fog turns to scalding steam and the front row leaves. Thorne opens a window without comment.|Too much water. A small rain falls on your desk, and only your desk, and on your hands, which are cold for an hour. Thorne writes something down.|You overshoot the line by a head and scald your wrist doing it. Thorne measures the fog with his stick, twice, in silence.}
opt.left.say.2 [d58808] = {火太多了。你的雾成了烫人的蒸汽，前排的人都撤了。索恩不发一言地打开了窗。|水太多了。一场小雨落在你的桌上，只落在你的桌上，还落在你手上，冷了一个小时。索恩记下了什么。|你的雾超线一个头，还烫着了手腕。索恩用尺量了两遍，一言不发。}
# en: Hold the water; let a partner burn
opt.right.label [aec9e6] = 你出水，搭档出火
# en: {You call the water and your partner warms it. Half the credit, half the effort, and all the mana you had.|You hold a ball of water steady for twenty minutes while your partner fusses with the flame. Your arms shake; your fog is fine.|You're the best water-holder in the class now, which Thorne calls "a respectable specialism" in a tone that isn't sure.}
opt.right.say.1 [2f4e68] = {你唤水，搭档加热。一半功劳，一半力气，外加你全部的法力。|搭档摆弄火苗的二十分钟里，你一直稳稳托着一团水。你的胳膊在抖；你们的雾没问题。|你如今是班上托水最稳的人，索恩称之为“一门体面的专长”，语气却拿不准。}

@event astro_dream_diary
# en: The Dream Diary
title [f68ac4] = 梦境日记
# en: {Every first-year astromancer keeps a dream diary, and once a month you read an entry aloud for the class to interpret. Today it's your turn.|Dream diaries again. The lecturer reminds you that dreams are evidence; the class reminds you they're also very funny.|Your turn with the dream diary. The class leans in; your entries have a following.} {Last night you dreamed about a goat in a crown.|Last night you dreamed your teeth were made of keys.|{season == "winter": Last night you dreamed of snow falling upward.|Last night you dreamed of an exam in a language made of birds.}}
text [1e4979] = {每个一年级星象学生都要记梦境日记，每月一次当众朗读一篇，让全班解梦。今天轮到你了。|又是梦境日记。讲师提醒你们梦是证据；全班提醒你们梦也非常好笑。|又轮到你读梦境日记了。全班凑了过来；你的日记有一批忠实读者。} {昨晚你梦见一只戴王冠的山羊。|昨晚你梦见自己的牙齿是钥匙做的。|{season == "winter": 昨晚你梦见雪往天上落。|昨晚你梦见一场用鸟语出题的考试。}}
# en: A circle of yawning students under an observatory dome, each holding a small notebook, one standing to read aloud while the others try not to laugh.
scene [c6085a] = 观星台穹顶下一圈打着哈欠的学生，人人手捧小本子，一个站起来朗读，其他人憋着不笑。
# en: Read the real one aloud
opt.left.label [ee46cd] = 读真实的那篇
# en: {You read about the goat. The class interprets it as ambition, appetite and possibly a farm. You go pink, and learn more than they do.|You read the dream of key-teeth. The lecturer finds three meanings in it; the class finds four, one of them rude.|You read it straight. The interpretations are thoughtful and humiliating, in equal parts.}
opt.left.say.1 [5b7285] = {你读了山羊那篇。全班解读为野心、食欲，可能还有一座农场。你脸红了，学到的却比他们多。|你读了钥匙牙齿的梦。讲师从中解出三层意思；全班解出四层，其中一层很粗俗。|你照实读了。解读既深刻又丢人，各占一半。}
# en: Invent something impressive
opt.right.label [8292d6] = 编个了不起的梦
# en: {You describe a dream of a silver hare on a staircase. The lecturer is deeply moved. You must remember to have it someday.|You invent a prophetic dream so convincing that half the class writes it down. The lecturer gives it full marks and a worried look.|Your invented dream gets a round of applause. You almost wish it were true.}
opt.right.say.1 [600d7b] = {你描述了一个梦：一只银色野兔站在楼梯上。讲师深受触动。你得记着哪天真梦一回。|你编了一个预言梦，逼真到半个班都记了下来。讲师给了满分，外加一个担忧的眼神。|你编的梦赢得了一阵掌声。你几乎希望它是真的。}
# en: {You get the silver hare's symbolism backwards. The lecturer, who keeps a book of real dream symbols, notices, and says so, gently, in front of everyone.|You overdo it. Nobody dreams in footnotes. The class is delighted to say so.|Halfway through, you forget what the hare was doing. The class finishes your dream for you, badly.}
opt.right.say.2 [07e04d] = {你把银色野兔的寓意说反了。讲师有一本真正的梦境符号书，她发现了，并且当着所有人温和地指了出来。|你编过头了。没人会梦见脚注。全班很乐意指出这一点。|讲到一半，你忘了那只野兔在干什么。全班替你把梦编完了，编得很糟。}

@event alch_antidote_race
# en: The Antidote Race
title [7842e3] = 解毒竞赛
# en: {Sister Amaranth sets a beaker of clear liquid in front of each pair. "A mild poison. Identify it. Counter it. Then drink both. Hourglass."|Antidote day. Sister Amaranth has made the poisons milder and the hourglass shorter.|The antidote race. You can smell three of Sister Amaranth's poisons from the door now; she has started using a fourth.} {The last pair to finish washes everyone's beakers.|One pair's tongues are already blue.|{season == "summer": The heat makes everything evaporate twice as fast.|Rain hammers the windows and nobody can hear the hourglass.}}
text [ea1dae] = {阿玛兰斯修女在每组面前放一烧杯清液。“轻微的毒。辨认它。解了它。然后两样都喝下去。沙漏。”|解毒日。阿玛兰斯修女把毒调得更轻，沙漏换得更短。|解毒竞赛。如今你在门口就能闻出阿玛兰斯修女的三种毒；她开始用第四种了。} {最后完成的那组要洗所有人的烧杯。|有一组人的舌头已经蓝了。|{season == "summer": 天热，什么都蒸发得快一倍。|雨点猛砸窗户，谁也听不见沙漏。}}
# en: A laboratory bench lined with beakers of clear liquid, each pair of students racing to identify and counter a mild poison while a healer watches an hourglass.
scene [da26fe] = 实验台上摆着一排装清液的烧杯，每组学生争分夺秒地辨认并化解一种轻微的毒，一位治疗师盯着沙漏。
# en: Identify it by testing
opt.left.label [b6e43b] = 靠试剂辨认
# en: {Three reagents and one colour change say hiccup-root. You counter it with mint and pepper and drink both before the sand's half gone. "Keep doing that," says Sister Amaranth.|You name it in two tests and brew the counter nearly blindfold. Sister Amaranth watches you drink without a word, which is praise.|You identify the fourth poison, the one she thought nobody would get. She looks at you over the hourglass and adds a fifth to her list.}
opt.left.say.1 [d6a8df] = {三种试剂，一次变色，说明是打嗝根。你用薄荷和胡椒解了它，沙子还没漏到一半就把两样都喝了。“保持下去。”阿玛兰斯修女说。|你两次检测就认了出来，几乎蒙着眼就调好了解药。阿玛兰斯修女看着你喝下去，一言不发，这就是夸奖。|你认出了第四种毒，就是她以为没人认得出的那种。她隔着沙漏看了你一眼，在单子上添了第五种。}
# en: {You guess wrong and drink a counter to the wrong thing. Your tongue is blue until supper.|You run out of sand, drink your best guess and hiccup in iambic rhythm for an hour.|Your antidote works on everything except the poison. Sister Amaranth hands you a second one, the right one, without comment.}
opt.left.say.2 [5ddd66] = {你猜错了，喝下了解另一种毒的药。你的舌头一直蓝到晚饭。|沙子漏完了，你喝下最好的猜测，按抑扬格的节奏打了一小时嗝。|你的解药什么都能解，除了这种毒。阿玛兰斯修女一言不发地递给你第二瓶，对的那瓶。}
# en: Brew a broad remedy instead
opt.right.label [fa70a8] = 改调一剂广谱药
# en: {You skip the testing and brew a remedy that counters most mild poisons, expensively. It works; it takes a lot out of you.|A broad remedy, slow and draining, and very safe. Sister Amaranth notes it as "a cautious answer", which is not praise.|Your broad remedy is so reliable now that the other pairs come to borrow it. Brewing it still leaves you hollow.}
opt.right.say.1 [6d2edc] = {你跳过检测，调了一剂能解大多数轻毒的药，代价不菲。管用；也掏空了你。|一剂广谱药，慢而耗神，非常稳妥。阿玛兰斯修女记下“谨慎的答案”，这可不是夸奖。|你的广谱药如今可靠到别组都来借。调它仍然让你浑身发虚。}

@event illu_turnip_market
# en: The Turnip Market
title [85c2c6] = 萝卜集市
# en: {Professor Vey gives everyone a turnip and a stall. "Glamour it into something I'll pay for. I have a purse of play-crowns, and no mercy."|Turnip market. Vey's purse of play-crowns is fatter this time, and so is her suspicion.|The turnip market again. Vey walks the stalls with her purse and the expression of a duchess at a bad auction.} {Your neighbour's turnip is already a very convincing tiara.|Somebody's ruby is dripping slightly.|{season == "autumn": The turnips are fresh from Old Maud's patch and smell of earth.|The hall smells overwhelmingly of turnip.}}
text [cb7975] = {维伊教授给每人发一个萝卜和一个摊位。“把它变成我愿意掏钱的东西。我有一袋游戏克朗，毫无怜悯之心。”|萝卜集市。维伊的游戏克朗钱袋这回更鼓了，她的疑心也是。|又是萝卜集市。维伊拎着钱袋在摊位间巡视，神情像个在糟糕拍卖会上的公爵夫人。} {你邻座的萝卜已经变成一顶以假乱真的冠冕。|有人的红宝石在微微滴水。|{season == "autumn": 萝卜是刚从老莫德菜地里拔的，带着泥土味。|大厅里萝卜味浓得化不开。}}
# en: Students at makeshift market stalls in a lecture hall holding up dazzling jewels that flicker, now and then, into turnips, while a theatrical professor drifts between them with a purse.
scene [2c666f] = 讲堂里搭起临时集市摊位，学生们举着璀璨的宝石，宝石时不时闪回萝卜原形，一位戏剧化的教授拎着钱袋在其间游走。
# en: Make it dazzle
opt.left.label [621304] = 让它光彩夺目
# en: {Your turnip becomes a sapphire the size of an egg. Vey turns it over, sniffs it, and pays three play-crowns. "It smells of turnip," she says. "I'll allow it."|You turn it into a golden pear. Vey bites it, which is cheating, then pays anyway, laughing.|Your turnip becomes a pocket watch that ticks. Vey listens to it and pays you double. "You made me want it," she says. "That's the whole art."}
opt.left.say.1 [4ad15a] = {你的萝卜变成一颗鸡蛋大的蓝宝石。维伊翻来覆去看了看，闻了闻，付了三个游戏克朗。“有萝卜味，”她说，“我认了。”|你把它变成一只金梨。维伊咬了一口，这是作弊，然后照样付钱，笑出了声。|你的萝卜变成一块滴答作响的怀表。维伊听了听，付了双倍。“你让我想要它，”她说，“这就是全部的艺术。”}
# en: {Your jewel flickers back into a turnip as Vey reaches for it. The whole hall sees. Vey pays you one play-crown, out of pity.|Your sapphire has roots. Vey points this out, delighted, to everyone.|Your watch ticks, then sprouts leaves. "Charming," says Vey, and moves on.}
opt.left.say.2 [57b3b4] = {维伊伸手时，你的宝石闪回了萝卜原形。整个大厅都看见了。维伊出于怜悯付了你一个游戏克朗。|你的蓝宝石长着根须。维伊兴高采烈地指给所有人看。|你的怀表滴答了几声，然后长出了叶子。“迷人，”维伊说着走开了。}
# en: Buy, and catch the fakes
opt.right.label [45b512] = 当买家，揪出假货
# en: {You're given a few play-crowns and set loose as a customer. You catch three turnips in disguise by their smell. Vey nods. "The other half of the art."|You haggle your way down the stalls and catch the dripping ruby out. Its maker sulks.|You can tell a glamoured turnip at ten paces now. Vey makes you her assistant buyer for the rest of the hour.}
opt.right.say.1 [6e9565] = {你拿到几个游戏克朗，被放出去当顾客。你凭气味揪出了三个伪装的萝卜。维伊点点头。“艺术的另一半。”|你一路砍价逛遍摊位，揪出了那颗滴水的红宝石。它的主人生起了闷气。|如今隔十步你就认得出施了魅影的萝卜。维伊让你当她的助理买手，直到下课。}

@event beast_bristle_trim
# en: The Bristle Trim
title [5b84c9] = 修剪扫帚尾
# en: {Professor Brask has the class trimming broom tails. "Broom's a creature. Sulky, stupid creature. Groom it, or it grooms you. Into a hedge."|Bristle day again. Brask inspects each broom tail like a hoof, muttering to the brooms more kindly than to you.|Broom trimming. Your school broom recognises you and shivers.} {A hippogriff watches from the paddock, judging.|One broom keeps flicking its twigs at whoever's trimming it.|{season == "winter": The twigs are brittle with frost and snap if you look at them.|The twigs are green and springy, and fight back.}}
text [ac9419] = {布拉斯克教授让全班修剪扫帚尾。“扫帚是生灵。又闷又蠢的生灵。你不打理它，它就打理你。打理进树篱里。”|又是修尾日。布拉斯克像检查马蹄一样检查每条扫帚尾，对扫帚嘟囔的话比对你们和气。|修剪扫帚。你的校用扫帚认出了你，打了个哆嗦。} {一头鹰头马身有翼兽在围场里看着，评头论足。|有把扫帚一直朝修剪它的人甩枝条。|{season == "winter": 枝条冻得发脆，你看它一眼就断。|枝条青绿有弹性，会还手。}}
# en: A row of school brooms clamped to a bench outside the stables, students with shears trimming and binding the twigs while a stern professor inspects each tail.
scene [ac23fc] = 马厩外一排校用扫帚夹在长凳上，学生们拿着剪子修剪捆扎枝条，一位严厉的教授挨个检查扫帚尾。
# en: Trim it twig by twig
opt.left.label [1799a9] = 一根一根地修
# en: {You bind every twig and trim the tail to a perfect curve. Brask looks it over. "Adequate. Broom thinks so too." Your fingers are numb, and the hour felt like three.|You trim for an hour, slowly, and your broom flies straighter for it. It's mindless and it isn't; your back aches.|You trim as Brask taught you, twig by twig. The broom purrs, if a broom can purr. Brask says it can. It's still the dullest hour of your week.}
opt.left.say.1 [9ddc8e] = {你捆好每根枝条，把尾巴修成完美的弧线。布拉斯克看了看。“还行。扫帚也这么觉得。”你的手指都麻了，这一小时像过了三小时。|你慢慢修了一小时，扫帚飞得更直了。这活儿说无脑也无脑，说不无脑也不无脑；你的背疼了。|你照布拉斯克教的，一根一根地修。扫帚发出呼噜声，如果扫帚会呼噜的话。布拉斯克说会。这仍是你一周里最无聊的一小时。}
# en: Test-fly it untrimmed
opt.right.label [06c2f1] = 不修就试飞
# en: {You fly it rough and it flies well anyway, the way some ugly ponies do. Brask watches, grunts, and lets you off.|The untrimmed broom bucks once and then settles under you like an old dog. Brask, drily: "Lucky. Don't count on it."|You know your broom's moods now; you fly it shaggy and it goes like a hawk. Brask almost smiles.}
opt.right.say.1 [5f36d9] = {你骑着毛糙的它飞，它照样飞得不错，就像有些丑小马一样。布拉斯克看着，哼了一声，放过了你。|没修的扫帚尥了一下蹶子，然后像条老狗一样在你身下安顿下来。布拉斯克淡淡地说：“走运。别指望。”|你如今摸透了扫帚的脾气；毛糙着飞，它也像鹰一样快。布拉斯克差点笑了。}
# en: {The shaggy tail catches the wind and you go into the hedge, as Brask predicted. She says so, to the hippogriff.|The broom sheds twigs in mid-air and spins you into the paddock. The hippogriff is unimpressed. So is Brask.|It bucks you off at head height. Brask tells the broom it did well, and tells you to get up.}
opt.right.say.2 [a43efa] = {毛糙的尾巴兜住了风，你一头扎进树篱，正如布拉斯克所料。她对那头鹰头马身有翼兽说了这话。|扫帚在半空掉枝条，把你转进了围场。鹰头马身有翼兽不为所动。布拉斯克也是。|它在一人高的地方把你甩了下来。布拉斯克夸扫帚干得好，叫你起来。}

@event umbral_shadow_witness
# en: The Shadow Witness
title [1d802b] = 影子证人
# en: {An inkpot has been taken from the professor's desk, on purpose, for the lesson. "The shadows in this room saw who took it," the professor says. "Ask them."|Another staged theft, a quill this time. The professor turns the lamps down. "Shadows remember. They just don't like being asked."|The shadow witness lesson. You know which corner's shadow gossips and which one sulks.} {The lamps burn low and blue.|The shadow under the window is longer than it should be.|{season == "winter": It's dark by mid-afternoon, and the shadows are bold.|A moth keeps throwing huge shadows across the ceiling, confusing everyone.}}
text [7cc732] = {教授桌上的墨水瓶被拿走了，这是故意的，为了上课。“这间屋里的影子看见了是谁拿的，”教授说，“去问它们。”|又一场布置好的失窃，这回是一支羽毛笔。教授把灯调暗。“影子会记得。它们只是不喜欢被问。”|影子证人课。你知道哪个角落的影子爱八卦，哪个爱赌气。} {灯火低低的，泛着蓝。|窗下的影子比它该有的长。|{season == "winter": 下午过半天就黑了，影子胆子很大。|一只飞蛾不停地把巨大的影子投到天花板上，把大家都弄糊涂了。}}
# en: A dim lecture room at the top of a tower, an empty desk with an inkpot-shaped gap in the dust, students crouching to question the long shadows in the corner.
scene [247446] = 塔顶昏暗的讲堂里，一张空桌的灰尘上留着墨水瓶形状的空白，学生们蹲下身盘问角落里的长影子。
# en: Question the long shadow
opt.left.label [fd07dc] = 盘问那道长影子
# en: {The long shadow leans toward the door, then toward a third-year's bag. The inkpot is in it. The professor nods. "Good. Shadows point. People lie."|You coax the shadow into showing a hand, a sleeve, a stride. You name the thief; the thief applauds.|The gossiping corner tells you everything before you've finished asking. The professor marks you down for leading the witness, and up for results.}
opt.left.say.1 [df26e7] = {长影子先朝门口倾斜，又朝一个三年级生的书包倾斜。墨水瓶就在里面。教授点点头。“很好。影子会指，人会撒谎。”|你哄影子显出一只手、一截袖子、一个步态。你指认了小偷；小偷鼓起了掌。|爱八卦的角落不等你问完就全说了。教授因你诱导证人扣分，又因你有结果加分。}
# en: {The shadow stretches toward you instead, and the cold of it settles in your hands. You name the wrong student, confidently.|The shadow shows you a thief who looks a great deal like the professor. The professor finds this very funny; you're freezing.|The sulking corner gives you nothing but chill. You spend the hour with numb fingers and no answer.}
opt.left.say.2 [2ae0a9] = {影子反而朝你伸过来，它的寒意钻进了你的手。你信心十足地指认错了人。|影子给你看的小偷长得非常像教授。教授觉得这很好笑；你冻僵了。|赌气的角落只给了你一身寒意。你一整节课手指冻麻，什么答案也没得到。}
# en: Watch the doorway, not the dark
opt.right.label [134e06] = 盯着门口，不看暗处
# en: {You ignore the shadows and work out who left the room and when. You get the right answer by the wrong method. The professor sighs, but marks it.|You reason it out from the dust on the desk. Correct, and entirely unmagical.|You solve it from the doorway again. The professor has started calling you "the magistrate", and doesn't mean it as a compliment.}
opt.right.say.1 [3274c9] = {你不理影子，推算出谁什么时候离开过房间。方法错了，答案对了。教授叹口气，还是给了分。|你从桌上的灰尘推理出来。正确，而且毫无魔法可言。|你又从门口解开了谜。教授开始叫你“地方法官”，而且不是在夸你。}

@event art_fair_entry
# en: Something for the Fair
title [23317b] = 参展作品
# en: {Every Artifice student is expected to have something for the Artificers' Fair. Yours is a clockwork wren that sings a little flat.|Fair entries again. Your wren now sings on key, mostly, and has started to hop.|Your fair entry has a name, a shelf and a temperament. The class has opinions about it.} {Your neighbour's entry, a self-pouring teapot, is pouring onto the floor.|Someone's entry has escaped and is hiding under the bench.|{season == "spring": The fair is weeks away and nobody is ready.|The fire buckets have been moved closer to the benches, on the faculty's orders.}}
text [d51fc9] = {每个奇械术学生都得为奇械博览会准备点东西。你的是一只唱歌有点跑调的发条鹪鹩。|又在准备参展作品。你的鹪鹩如今大致唱得准了，还开始蹦跳。|你的参展作品有了名字、一个架子和一副脾气。全班对它各有意见。} {你邻座的作品，一把会自己倒茶的茶壶，正往地上倒。|有人的作品逃跑了，躲在工作台底下。|{season == "spring": 离展会还有几周，谁都没准备好。|按教职员的命令，消防水桶挪得离工作台更近了。}}
# en: A workshop bench crowded with half-built clockwork entries for the Artificers' Fair, a student holding a tiny screwdriver over a machine that twitches.
scene [046c89] = 工坊的工作台上挤满了为奇械博览会准备的半成品发条作品，一个学生拿着一把小螺丝刀悬在一台抽搐着的机器上方。
# en: Tinker with your own
opt.left.label [1b58cd] = 调校自己的作品
# en: {You adjust the wren's voice-reed by a hair and it sings a whole scale. The workshop goes quiet to listen.|The wren hops, sings and flutters, and nothing catches fire. That's the bar, and you've cleared it.|You get the wren to sing something nobody built into it. You don't know how. You write it down very fast.}
opt.left.say.1 [b6983a] = {你把鹪鹩的发声簧片调了一丝，它唱出了完整的音阶。整个工坊安静下来聆听。|鹪鹩蹦着、唱着、扑腾着，什么也没着火。这就是及格线，你过了。|你让鹪鹩唱出了一段谁也没给它装进去的旋律。你不知道是怎么回事。你飞快地记了下来。}
# en: {The wren sings one perfect note and then smokes. Your fingers are singed from catching it.|You fix the flat note and break the hop. The wren lurches round the bench like a drunk sparrow. You burn a thumb on the spring.|The wren sings, beautifully, and then won't stop. You have to pull a gear with smoking pliers to get some peace, and burn yourself doing it.}
opt.left.say.2 [97cd04] = {鹪鹩唱出一个完美的音，然后冒起了烟。你接住它时烫伤了手指。|你修好了跑调，却弄坏了蹦跳。鹪鹩像只醉麻雀一样在工作台上东倒西歪。你被弹簧烫了拇指。|鹪鹩唱得很美，然后停不下来。你只好用冒烟的钳子拔掉一个齿轮才得清静，还烫着了自己。}
# en: Rescue the neighbour's entry
opt.right.label [201236] = 抢救邻座的作品
# en: {You stop the teapot pouring, rebind its spout-charm and dry the floor. Your own wren waits, unfinished, all hour. Your neighbour will owe you for life.|You coax the escaped entry out from under the bench and fix its leg. Your wren sulks on its shelf, untouched.|You spend the hour on someone else's machine again. Theirs works now. Yours sings flat.}
opt.right.say.1 [729187] = {你让茶壶停止倒茶，重新绑好壶嘴咒，擦干地板。你自己的鹪鹩没完工，等了一整节课。邻座这辈子都欠你的。|你把逃跑的作品从工作台底下哄出来，修好了它的腿。你的鹪鹩在架子上生闷气，没人碰它。|你又把一节课花在了别人的机器上。他们的能用了。你的还在跑调。}

@event star_cloudy_appointment
# en: A Cloudy Appointment
title [f922c1] = 阴天的约课
# en: {Tonight's appointment, says this morning's note, will go ahead "whatever the sky thinks". The sky thinks clouds, wall to wall.|Another clouded appointment tonight. The note is unbothered. "Starlight comes through cloud. It simply has to want to."|Cloud again tonight. You know the dome's cold corners and which way the gaps will drift.} {Somewhere behind the murk, the star you know best will be up.|The note says a thin gap may open in the west.|{season == "winter": It will be snow-cloud, heavy and low; your breath will freeze on the rail.|It will be warm cloud, with rain coming.}}
text [fd4a83] = {今早的字条说，今晚的课“不管天空怎么想”都照常进行。天空想的是云，铺天盖地。|又一个阴天的约课。字条上的语气毫不在意。“星光能穿透云层。它只需要愿意。”|今晚又是云。你知道穹顶里哪个角落冷，云缝会往哪边飘。} {在那片阴霾后面，你最熟悉的那颗星会升起来。|字条说西边可能会开一道细缝。|{season == "winter": 会是低沉厚重的雪云；你的呼吸会冻在栏杆上。|会是暖云，雨正在来。}}
# en: A brass observatory dome open to a heavy, clouded night sky, a student reaching up with both hands toward a faint gleam behind the clouds.
scene [f5326a] = 黄铜观星穹顶朝着厚重的阴云夜空敞开，一个学生伸出双手，够向云后一抹微光。
# en: Call through the cloud
opt.left.label [6918ba] = 穿云唤星
# en: {The starlight comes down through the cloud like a rope through water, slow and then all at once. Your palms glow till dawn.|You call, and the cloud thins over your hands alone, a little round window in the sky. The lecturer writes for a long time.|You call the star by name and it answers, cloud or no cloud. You walk back down the stairs with light still in your fingers.}
opt.left.say.1 [1810fd] = {星光像绳子穿过水一样穿过云层降下来，先慢，然后一下子全到了。你的掌心一直亮到天明。|你一唤，云只在你手上方变薄，天上开了一扇小小的圆窗。讲师写了很久。|你叫出那颗星的名字，它应了，不管有没有云。你走下楼梯时，手指里还有光。}
# en: {You call until your hands shake. The cloud doesn't care. You go to bed drained and dark.|A thread of light comes halfway and frays in the murk. It takes something out of you as it goes.|You reach up for an hour into nothing. The lecturer says even nothing is a lesson. It doesn't feel like one.}
opt.left.say.2 [5ad4c4] = {你唤到双手发抖。云毫不在乎。你上床时又累又暗。|一缕光降到一半，在阴霾里散开了。它走时带走了你的一些东西。|你朝着虚空伸手伸了一个小时。讲师说就连虚空也是一课。感觉可不像。}
# en: Chart the gaps in the cloud
opt.right.label [fafc06] = 绘制云缝图
# en: {You sit by the rail all night logging the gaps, when and where and which stars peeked through. Cold to the bone; good data.|You chart the drift of the cloud like a sailor and predict the next gap to the minute. It comes; you're too frozen to cheer.|Your cloud log is pages long now. You know the sky's habits even when you can't see it, and your chest aches with cold.}
opt.right.say.1 [b00704] = {你在栏杆边坐了一整夜，记录云缝：何时、何处、哪些星探出了头。冷到骨头里；数据很好。|你像水手一样绘出云的漂移，把下一道缝预测到了分钟。它来了；你冻得欢呼不出来。|你的云层日志如今已有好几页。就算看不见天，你也摸清了它的习性，胸口冷得发疼。}

@event hollow_jarred_silences
# en: Silences in Jars
title [12282e] = 罐中的寂静
# en: {Today the headmistress hands you an empty jar. "Seal a silence in it. Not quiet; silence. You will know the difference by the end."|Another empty jar. Behind the headmistress, a shelf of stoppered jars, all apparently empty, all labelled in faded hands.|Silence jars. You know the weight of a well-sealed one now, heavier than it looks.} {The lamp hisses.|The books on the shelves have stopped breathing, as if to help.|{final_year: She asks what silence you'd keep, if you could keep only one.|She works at her own jar, unhurried, while you work at yours.}}
text [b7f096] = {今天院长递给你一只空罐子。“把一段寂静封进去。不是安静；是寂静。到最后你会知道其中的区别。”|又一只空罐子。院长身后有一架塞着瓶塞的罐子，看上去全是空的，标签的字迹都已褪色。|寂静罐。如今你知道一只封好的罐子有多沉，比看上去沉。} {灯在嘶嘶作响。|架上的书停止了呼吸，像是在帮忙。|{final_year: 她问你，如果只能留一段寂静，你会留哪一段。|她不紧不慢地封着自己的罐子，你封你的。}}
# en: A windowless room lined with black-bound books and a shelf of small stoppered jars, each holding nothing visible, a student holding one up to the lamplight.
scene [37a5d9] = 一间没有窗户的屋子，四壁排满黑皮书，一架小小的塞着瓶塞的罐子里看不见任何东西，一个学生把其中一只举到灯下。
# en: Seal the room's silence
opt.left.label [62c333] = 封存这间屋的寂静
# en: {You draw the room's silence into the jar a breath at a time and stopper it. When you shake it, nothing happens, very heavily. She nods.|The silence fights the stopper like a cat fights a bath. You win, eventually, emptied out.|You seal a silence so clean that the lamp seems louder when you're done. The headmistress takes the jar and shelves it with the old ones.}
opt.left.say.1 [79f708] = {你一口气一口气地把屋里的寂静吸进罐子，塞上瓶塞。摇一摇，什么也没发生，沉甸甸地什么也没发生。她点点头。|寂静像猫抗拒洗澡一样抗拒瓶塞。你最终赢了，人也被掏空了。|你封了一段如此纯净的寂静，封完后灯声似乎都响了。院长接过罐子，和那些旧罐子摆在一起。}
# en: Unseal one of the old jars
opt.right.label [f5213c] = 打开一只旧罐子
# en: {You unstopper a jar dated a century ago. Out comes the silence of a room just after someone laughed. It's unbearably sad, and you don't know why.|You open an old jar and the room fills with the silence of a held breath before a goodbye. You close it again quickly. She says nothing, kindly.|You open one more old jar. A silence after snow. You sit in it a long while before you can speak.}
opt.right.say.1 [004de2] = {你拔开一只一百年前的罐子。放出来的是有人刚笑过之后的屋子里的寂静。悲伤得让人受不了，你却不知为何。|你打开一只旧罐子，屋里充满了告别前屏住呼吸的寂静。你赶紧又封上。她什么也没说，很体贴。|你又打开一只旧罐子。雪后的寂静。你在里面坐了很久，才说得出话。}
